WHAT THIS MEANS IN PLAIN WORDS
------------------------------
  * If you CHANGE a file of Firn -- the compiler, the standard library,
    the code generator -- and pass your version on, you must publish those
    changed files. A fork of the language stays open.
  * If you only USE Firn to write your own program, that program is yours.
    It may be closed and it may be sold. Nothing rubs off on it.

This is the same trade Mozilla makes for Firefox, and it is the reason MPL
was chosen over the GPL: a language lives from being used.

